nodecode-edinet is a rewrite of TakeshiTGAL's TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-edinet:

  https://github.com/TakeshiTGAL/hermes-plugin-edinet
  commit 06171c84b23ab5e35b0c58203cebcbee33117110
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 TakeshiTGAL (LICENSE)

The plugin was three tools over the EDINET API v2 — edinet_search_filings,
edinet_financials and edinet_save_document — a stdlib HTTP client, a disk
cache of each file date's list, a parser for the type=5 CSV ZIP, and one
skill that told the model to reach for the tools before a web search. This
rewrite keeps the three tools, their names, their arguments, the same two
GETs to api.edinet-fsa.go.jp with the key in the Subscription-Key query
parameter, the same filters applied locally, the same taxonomy element ids
per headline figure, the same refusals (a date range over the cap errors
instead of truncating; a figure with no matching row is reported missing,
never invented), the same citation line with the filing page and PDL 1.0,
and the skill, as (help :edinet). It is written against Nodecode's own seams
(nlk:http, a section, a contract per tool), so no Hermes runtime, no
manifest and no private Hermes modules are needed, and the CSV ZIP is read
here: the central directory is parsed directly and CHIPZ inflates the member.

Left out: the plugin's disk cache of list responses (15 minutes for today,
24 hours for a past date, keyed by a hash of the API key), so a repeated
search asks EDINET again — the section's pace_seconds still keeps the
requests a second apart; the plugin's same-host redirect guard, because
nlk:http follows a redirect itself; its retry of 429 and 5xx (a refusal
says to wait and call again); the plugin's private agent.file_safety and
plugins.plugin_storage modules, replaced by the Nodecode home; and the
tool-level max_calendar_days argument, which the section's own
max_calendar_days governs here. The corporate-number example in the
plugin's messages is kept as it was.

EDINET data belongs to the Financial Services Agency of Japan: the terms
(WZEK0030) ask for the source citation every answer carries, and the
taxonomy is quoted under PDL 1.0. EDINET, 金融庁: https://disclosure2.edinet-fsa.go.jp/
